                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I was hoping for a modern recreation of the old retro game Joust, but unfortunately the quality of the implementation of this game is so extremely bad that I find it almost impossible to enjoy it at all.\n\nThere was clearly very little attention to quality control applied when making and releasing this game.\n\nIt is rife from top to bottom with bugs and inconsistencies. \n\nThis is the opposite of a game that has had love and polish put into it. It is like what you would expect from a student game jam except even buggier and lower quality than average even for that context.\n\nTLDR: This game is so poorly implemented that it is completely unprofessional and unworthy of public sale. No self respecting game developer should ever release a product whose quality control is this poor and careless.\n\nLook elsewhere if you want a Joust-like game. I promise you that you almost certainly won't enjoy this one. It's a shame too, since it could have been good in theory.",
